<!-- DAC EXPLANATION AND USE CASES -->
<section style="padding: 50px 20px 30px; margin-bottom: 40px; max-width: 96%; background-color: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 30px; color: #003C78; text-align: center;">Introducing Direct Air Capture</h2>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 30px;">

        <!-- What is DAC -->
        <div class="hover-frame" style="flex: 1 1 300px; max-width: 600px; background: white; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
            <h3 style="color: #003C78; margin-top: 0;">What is Direct Air Capture?</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">Direct Air Capture (DAC) is a technology that removes CO₂ directly from the ambient air. The captured CO₂ can then be permanently stored underground or reused in industrial processes. DAC systems typically use chemical solutions or solid sorbents to bind atmospheric CO₂, followed by processes that release and concentrate it for storage.</p>
            <img src="img/dac_diagram.png" alt="DAC Cycle" style="width: 100%; margin-top: 15px; border-radius: 8px;" />

        </div>

<!-- Pioneering Project: Climeworks -->
<div class="hover-frame" style="flex: 1 1 300px; max-width: 500px; min-height: 480px; background: white; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3 style="color: #003C78; margin-top: 0;">Climeworks – Scaling DAC</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">Climeworks, a Swiss company, is a global leader in DAC deployment. Their Iceland-based plant “Orca” is one of the first commercial-scale facilities removing CO₂ from air and storing it underground using geothermal energy and mineralization.</p>
    <img src="img/climeworks.jpg" alt="Climeworks DAC Plant" style="width: 100%; margin-top: 15px; border-radius: 8px;" />
</div>

<!-- Pioneering Project: Carbon Engineering -->
<div class="hover-frame" style="flex: 1 1 300px; max-width: 500px; min-height: 480px; background: white; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <h3 style="color: #003C78; margin-top: 0;">Carbon Engineering – Large-scale Vision</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">Based in Canada, Carbon Engineering is developing industrial-scale DAC plants capable of removing up to one million tons of CO₂ per year. They emphasize integration with low-carbon energy sources and CO₂ utilization options.</p>
    <img src="img/carbonengineering.jpg" alt="Carbon Engineering Facility" style="width: 100%; margin-top: 15px; border-radius: 8px;" />
</div>

    </div>
</section>

